What:           /sys/bus/platform/drivers/vdec/.../isolated
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        linux-media@vger.kernel.org
Description:
                Read-only quarantine state for the Amlogic T7 encoder. 0 is
                not quarantined (also check recovering), 1 means that recovery
                from a command/frame/cancellation failure failed. All old queues
                report errors and new opens
                and hardware jobs are rejected. DMA memory and mappings are
                retained because stopping DMA has not been established. The
                module cannot be unloaded and userspace unbind is disabled.
                Only a board reboot clears a failed recovery. A KOBJ_CHANGE
                uevent carries
                WAVE5_ISOLATED=1 when quarantine is published.

What:           /sys/bus/platform/drivers/vdec/.../recovering
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        linux-media@vger.kernel.org
Description:
                Read-only recovery state for the Amlogic T7 encoder. 1 means
                new opens and hardware jobs are blocked while all old queues
                are failed and the driver attempts a drained power cycle of
                the dedicated domain followed by a cold firmware reload.
                Success clears recovering and emits WAVE5_RECOVERED=1 in a
                KOBJ_CHANGE uevent; old file handles remain failed and must be
                closed and reopened. Failure sets isolated to 1, keeps DMA
                storage pinned and emits WAVE5_ISOLATED=1 instead.

What:           /sys/bus/platform/drivers/vdec/.../isolation_reason
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        linux-media@vger.kernel.org
Description:
                Read-only human-readable initiating failure, or "none" before
                a failure. Retained after successful recovery; updated on the
                next recovery attempt. Nested failures do not replace it.

What:           /sys/bus/platform/drivers/vdec/.../isolation_time_ns
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        linux-media@vger.kernel.org
Description:
                Read-only decimal CLOCK_BOOTTIME nanoseconds at the initiating
                failure, or 0 before failure. This is not wall-clock time.
